      "title": "Caritas Bianchi College of Careers",
      "description": "Saint Francis University - Caritas Bianchi College of Careers Caritas Bianchi College of Careers The Irene Lam Department of Design offers the following programmes: Higher Diploma in Design (Full-time) [SSSDP] Higher Diploma in Film and Media Production (Full-time) [SSSDP] The Faith Hope Love Department of General Education offers the following programmes: Higher Diploma in Music Studies (Full-time) Diploma in Foundation Studies of Higher Education (Full-time)"
    },
    "https://repository.cihe.edu.hk/jspui/": {
      "title": "",
      "description": "Skip to main content Research Outputs Researchers Schools Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages Rita Tong Liu School of Business and Hospitality Management S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences Yam Pak Charitable Foundation School of Computing and Information Sciences Help SFU Institutional Repository The Institutional Repository is a scholarly research network of SFU, which archives a collection of staff publications that are accessible to all members of SFU. At the moment, the Institutional Repository houses publications that came out from recent years. More and more research papers will be added to the databases on a continuous basis. To update your latest research outputs, please fill out the Collection Form for Staff Publications . Search Loading... Recent Additions Loading... Most viewed Loading... Responsible Use of E‑Resources | Privacy Policy | Disclaimer © SFU Library. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://www.sfu.edu.hk/en/career/deanship-headship-positions/index.html": {
      "title": "Deanship / Headship Positions",
      "description": "Saint Francis University - Deanship / Headship Positions Deanship / Headship Positions Notes For Applicants: Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested parties are invited to submit: a written application indicating expected salary; a CV; and a duly completed application form . Please email to hrm@sfu.edu.hk before the application deadline. Candidates not invited for interview within 2 months after the application deadline may assume their applications unsuccessful. Download Application Form here All personal data provided by the applicants will be treated in strict confidence and used only for recruitment and employment-related purposes. Deanship / Headship Positions Director of Finance & Estates Office (Ref.: 26/90/FEO/D) Duties Lead and manage the FEO, ensuring efficient delivery of core operational functions including budgeting and financial planning, financial accounting, income collection and recording, payment processing, procurement and purchase requisitions, resource allocation, property and estate management, and general office administration. Provide strategic direction for financial planning and resource management, aligning resource allocation with university priorities and long-term objectives. Ensure the integrity of financial reporting and compliance with applicable accounting standards, statutory requirements and internal controls. Oversee income collection procedures to maximise revenue accuracy and timeliness. Lead procurement and payments processes, implementing best practices to ensure compliance with the financial management policies and maintaining appropriate controls. Oversee the University's property management and estate functions, monitoring the Property Management Office as well as external contractors and service providers to ensure standards and regulatory compliance. Develop, review and maintain robust policies, guidelines and procedures across finance, procurement, resource allocation and estates management to promote good governance and operational efficiency. Prepare proposals, project planning, budgets and other necessary documentation for campus development and capital projects; and coordinate with internal and external stakeholders as required. Lead or contribute to major capital project governance, including budget oversight, financial modelling, risk assessment and reporting. Provide advice to senior leadership on financial implications of strategic initiatives and campus development options. Mentor, develop and build capacity within the FEO team to ensure high performance and succession planning. Undertake ad hoc assignments and special projects as requested by the Vice-President (Finance & Institutional Advancement). Appointment Criteria Applicants should meet the following criteria: Possess a recognized master's degree or above level in accounting, finance, business administration, or a related discipline; Possess a professional accounting qualification (e.g. HKCPA); Possess significant post-qualification experience in senior finance, estates or resources management roles, preferably within higher education, the public sector or large organisations; Possess substantive knowledge of financial management, budgeting, accounting standards and procurement practices; Have demonstrated experience in managing capital or campus development projects, including preparation of business cases and financial models; Have excellent leadership and people management skills, with proven experience building and leading multidisciplinary teams; Have strong stakeholder management and communication skills, with the ability to liaise effectively with academic and administrative leaders, external consultants and regulatory bodies; and Have high integrity, sound judgement and a strong commitment to good governance. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Director of Student Affairs (Ref.: 26/75/SAO/D) Duties The Director of Student Affairs will assist the University in formulating, implementing and reviewing systems, strategies and plans for student development and support. The appointee will head the Student Affairs Office with a team of professional staff and oversee the provision of co-curriculum including whole-person development, service learning, sport development, global exposure, counseling, support for non-local and SEN students, career planning and guidance, alumni affairs etc… He/ She is also expected to act as a liaison person between students and the University, and work closely with academic schools/ departments, administrative units and student groups to cultivate a campus environment conductive to teaching, learning, campus life and wellness. Appointment Criteria Good academic and professional qualifications, preferably at a post-graduate degree level; Proven track record of management experience and serving youth in the tertiary education setting; Excellent communication, interpersonal, problem solving and negotiation skills; and Proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled"
    },
    "https://www.sfu.edu.hk/en/career/senior-management-positions/index.html": {
      "title": "Senior Management Positions",
      "description": "Saint Francis University - Senior Management Positions Senior Management Positions Notes For Applicants: Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested parties are invited to submit: a written application indicating expected salary; a CV; and a duly completed application form . Please email to hrm@sfu.edu.hk before the application deadline. Candidates not invited for interview within 2 months after the application deadline may assume their applications unsuccessful. Download Application Form here All personal data provided by the applicants will be treated in strict confidence and used only for recruitment and employment-related purposes. Senior Management Positions"
    },
    "https://www.sfu.edu.hk/en/career/administrative-services-positions/index.html": {
      "title": "Administrative / Services Positions",
      "description": "Saint Francis University - Administrative / Services Positions Administrative / Services Positions Notes For Applicants: Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested parties are invited to submit: a written application indicating expected salary; a CV; and a duly completed application form Please email to: hrm@sfu.edu.hk before the application deadline. Candidates not invited for interview within 2 months after the application deadline may assume their applications unsuccessful. Download Application Form here All personal data provided by the applicants will be treated in strict confidence and used only for recruitment and employment-related purposes. Administrative / Services Positions Project Manager, QESS Project (Value and Ethics Education through Chinese Culture Promotion Project) (Ref.: 26/123/QESS/PM) Duties The successful candidate will be responsible for (a) providing management and oversees the implementation of the whole project, (b) ensuring the on-time implementation of the deliverables, liaises with different parties (academic and supporting units) in promoting Chinese cultural activities, coordinates training activities, organizes publicity events and manages the budget and progress of the project. (c) working closely with other Chinese culture promotion organization in our community or in the Greater Bay Area, (d) supervising and collaborating with the administrative officer to ensure the smooth implementation of all the deliverables and ensures the optimum attainment of the project objective, (e) being an advisor of the Chinese Culture Student Ambassador Team. Appointment Criteria Applicants should (a) have a recognised bachelor's degree or above qualification, preferably experienced in project management; (b) have relevant experience of promoting Chinese Culture related activities; (c) have a mature and pleasant personality with good team spirit, communication skills and interpersonal relationship, be proactive in work and able to work independently, efficiently and responsibly; (d) have a good command of both spoken and written English and Chinese (Cantonese and Putonghua); (e) be proficient in computer skills. Application Deadline 15/09/2026 Administrative Officer, QESS Project (Value and Ethics Education through Chinese Culture Promotion Project) (Ref.: 26/122/QESS/AO) Duties The appointee will be required to (a) support the Project Manager to ensure smooth and on-time implementation of the project objectives and deliverables; (b) promotion of activities and connecting with the external guests or NGOs; (c) provide administrative support for the project; (d) provide secretarial support for the project. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognised Bachelor's degree; (b) a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); (c) proficiency in computer applications; (d) good organizational and communication skills; and (e) relevant work experience. Application Deadline 15/09/2026 Associate/ Assistant Director, Information Technology Services Centre (Ref.: 26/121/ITSC/AD) Duties The appointee will be responsible for assisting the Director of Information Technology Services Centre (ITSC), for managing the day-to-day operations of the Centre. Assist the University's overarching IT strategy, driving innovation and ensuring alignment with long-term objectives. Supervise the technology vision, strategy, and execution of digital services platform for operational excellence with continuous improvement. Lead, manage, mentor, and develop IT teams; handle workforce planning, performance management, recruitment, and foster a culture of innovation, continuous improvement. Supervise all aspects of computer operations, ensuring efficient delivery of core operational functions including managing and delivering IT infrastructure, computer systems to fulfill institute's IT strategies and direction. Develop, review, and maintain a robust framework of IT policies, controls, and procedures to ensure the availability, confidentiality, and integrity of data across the entire Institution. Contribute to budgeting, resource allocation, and financial oversight of IT operations and projects. Participate as member in meetings of the respective committees as and when necessary. Deputize for the Director of ITSC and perform other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have: (i) preferably with a recognized postgraduate degree in Computer Science, Information Technology or related disciplines; (ii) at least 10 years' relevant experience, preferably in a similar position in local/ overseas higher education institutions; at least 4 years of IT experience with significant leadership responsibility (iii) sound technical background, a generalist of IT technologies and also a specialist on core technologies; (iv) strong team and vendor management; (v) good communication and problem solving skills; and (vi) a good command of spoken and written English and Chinese. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Assistant Registrar, Registry (Ref.: 26/117/REG/AR) Duties Reporting to the Registrar, the appointee will be responsible for (a) assisting the Registrar in providing strategic leadership and direction for Registry operations and academic administration; (b) overseeing designated functional areas within the Registry and ensuring the effective management of staff, resources, and service delivery; (c) spearheading the digital transformation of Registry services through the development, implementation, and continuous enhancement of administrative systems, workflow automation, and technology-enabled solutions; (d) reviewing and optimizing business processes, policies, and procedures to enhance operational effectiveness and service excellence; (e) overseeing the administration of academic regulations, student records, examinations, graduation, quality assurance, and other Registry-related functions as assigned; (f) preparing institutional reports, statistical analyses, and management information to support governance and strategic planning; (g) fostering effective collaboration with internal and external stakeholders to ensure the successful implementation of policies, systems, and projects; (h) supporting committee work and providing professional advice on academic administration, governance, and regulatory matters; (i) leading special projects and initiatives to support the University's strategic development; and (j) performing any other duties as assigned by the Registrar. Appointment Criteria Applicants should (a) hold a Bachelor's degree, preferably a Master's degree, with a minimum of 15 years of relevant full-time post-qualification experience, including at least 5 years in a leadership role within a higher education setting; (b) demonstrate a strong IT and system development background, with proven experience in leading or participating in the development, enhancement, implementation, and optimization of administrative systems and digital solutions to improve operational efficiency, service delivery, and business processes; (c) demonstrate strong organizational and interpersonal skills; (d) possess excellent communication abilities with a high level of proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese; (e) exhibit a proven capacity to work independently and efficiently under tight deadlines, while managing multiple tasks in an organized manner; (f) demonstrate effective teamwork skills, be self-motivated, and capable of performing well under pressure; and (g) preferably have experience working in the Registry of local self-financing tertiary education institutions. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Assistant Library Officer (Access Services), Library (Ref.: 26/113/LIB/ALO) Duties The appointee will be required to (1) discharge operational duties relating to circulation services, information enquiries, shelving, collections and facilities maintenance; (2) provide technical and administrative support and collate statistical data on the circulation of library materials; (3) assist in managing course readings; (4) offer assistance to library patrons in the use of services and facilities; (5) help with the supervision of part-time Library Assistants; (6) work at service counters on a shift basis, including at evenings and on weekends; and (7) carry out other duties as assigned by the supervisors or the University Librarian. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (1) a recognized Degree or Higher Diploma, preferably in library information management related disciplines; (2) a familiarity with the academic library systems and discovery services; (3) experience in providing circulation and information services in an academic library setting; (4) a reasonably high level of proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); and (5) an ability to work independently and/ or within a team and to perform duties in a self-motivated, collegial and responsible manner. Fresh graduates are welcome to apply, but preference will be given to applicants who are conversant with academic library operations. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Assistant Library Officer (Acquisitions), Library (Ref.: 26/112/LIB/ALO) Duties The appointee will be required to (1) assist in the acquisition of library materials in both print and electronic formats, undertaking tasks including placing and receiving orders as well as handling payment transactions; (2) provide technical and administrative support, and compile statistical data related to acquisitions; (3) discharge operational duties relating to circulation services, information enquiries, shelving and collections maintenance; (4) work at service counters on a shift basis, including at evenings and on weekends; and (5) carry out other duties as assigned by the supervisors or the University Librarian. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (1) a recognized Degree or Higher Diploma, preferably in library information management related disciplines; (2) a familiarity with the academic library systems and discovery services; (3) a reasonably high level of proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); (4) an ability to work independently and/ or within a team and to perform duties in a self-motivated, collegial and responsible manner. Fresh graduates are welcome to apply, but preference will be given to applicants who are conversant with academic library operations. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Public Affairs Officer (Communications), Public Affairs Office (Ref.: 26/108/PAO/PAO) Duties The appointee will be required to: Draft, edit and coordinate press releases, speeches, newspaper op-eds, brochures, newsletters, annual reports and other communications materials in both English and Chinese; Identify and develop newsworthy stories about the University's achievements, initiatives and people, and assist in pitching them to the media; Assist in maintaining media relations and responding to media enquiries; Monitor and analyse media coverage, and prepare regular reports on media sentiment and public perception of the University; Assist in organising media visits, publicity events, stakeholder engagement and community outreach programmes; Support the implementation of the Public Affairs Office's corporate communications, branding and publicity strategies; Maintain media lists, communications records and relevant databases; and Perform any other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should possess: A recognised degree, preferably in journalism, communications, marketing, public relations or a related discipline; At least three years of relevant working experience in communications, public relations, marketing or a related field; Experience in news media or media relations will be a definite advantage; Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; Strong writing, editing and interpersonal skills; Proficiency in word processing, presentation software, digital communications tools and AI applications; The ability to work effectively with different stakeholders and manage multiple tasks under tight deadlines; and Good organisational and project coordination skills. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Project Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences   (Ref.: 26/107/HS/PA) Duties To support the administrative work and deployment of the project To assist in handling documents and promotional materials arising from the project, including the progress report To coordinate and assist in the implementation of the system in the hosting institution To coordinate the promotion, training and sharing session of the system to students and academic staff in the hosting institution To assist in collecting user experience feedback surveys To serve as the contact person of Saint Francis University (SFU) to liaise with the project team members, academics, clinical experts, service providers and vendors in facilitating and developing the scenarios, software and hardware facilities Appointment Criteria A Bachelor's degree in Health, Education, Psychology or Computing Sciences or related discipline, or equivalent qualification Have a strong sense of responsibility and self-motivation Good command of English and Chinese is an advantage Good organizational and interpersonal skills with cultural sensitivity Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Senior Laboratory Technician, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences  (Ref.: 26/106/HS/SLT) Duties Assist supervisor of the nursing faculty to implement the skills laboratory curriculum. This includes the use of a variety of patient care equipment and supplies. Assist supervisor in developing the system to ensure all laboratory equipment is properly maintained and functioning in relation to manufacturer's recommendations. Function as a team head for laboratory technicians to deliver efficient support for the daily operation of nurse labs. Organize nursing lab team members to set up all skills labs, practice sessions, and on-campus labs offered in all nursing courses. Sustain the electronic booking system to schedule skill practice sessions for all nursing students. Ensure the availability of properly functioning equipment and supplies; maintain warranties and renewals for all equipment; perform routine equipment repair. Monitor inventory of all laboratory supplies and equipment in the nurse labs. Provide orientation and skill training for new recruit / junior lab technicians. Oversee laboratory maintenance, safety, and handling of hazardous wastes. Assess laboratory space to ensure compliance with OSHA and other regulatory agencies. Provide instruction related to the use of laboratory equipment and nursing practice and procedures. Organize and arrange simulation practice including lifting and transporting manikins and equipment. Appointment Criteria A recognised Bachelor's or above in Nursing Studies or equivalent, preferably having practised as Enrolled / Registered Nurse. Working experience in providing nursing care is preferred. Two years' working experience in a health-care related institution / organization. Experience in managing stock and inventory with electronic system. Proficiency in written and spoken English and Chinese (preferably including Putonghua). Good communication, interpersonal and organisational skills. Self-initiative and the ability to work independently. Able to work shift duty (no night duty). Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Administrative Officer (5-month Maternity Cover, contract start from Sep 2026 - Feb 2027), Registry (Ref.: 26/104/REG/AO/TEMP) Duties The appointee will be responsible for supporting the Registry's daily operations, including student admission, registration, enrolment, assessment, graduation, record management, liaison with internal and external parties, institute promotion, and other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognised Bachelor's degree; (b) at least 2 years' relevant work experience; (c) a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); (d) proficiency in computer applications; and (e) good analytical, communication and organisational skills, with a proactive attitude, a strong sense of responsibility, and good team spirit. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Administrative Officer, Registry (Ref.: 26/103/REG/AO) Duties The appointee will be responsible for supporting the Registry's daily operations, including student admission, registration, enrolment, assessment, graduation, record management, liaison with internal and external parties, institute promotion, and other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognised Bachelor's degree; (b) at least 2 years' relevant work experience; (c) a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); (d) proficiency in computer applications; and (e) good analytical, communication and organisational skills, with a proactive attitude, a strong sense of responsibility, and good team spirit. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled [Full-time] Administrative Officer, Rita Tong Liu School of Business and Hospitality Management (Ref.: 26/102/BHM/AO) Duties The role involves providing comprehensive administrative support for programme operations while effectively liaising with both internal and external parties. Responsibilities include offering assistance for committee meetings and managing logistics arrangements, which encompass materials preparation, participant coordination, and on-site support for various events and school initiatives. Additionally, the position requires performing any other duties as assigned, ensuring the smooth execution of all related tasks. Appointment Criteria Applicants should possess (a) a recognized Bachelor's degree; (b) at least two years of experience in planning and executing events such as conferences, workshops, or corporate gatherings, including managing logistics, budgets, and vendor coordination; (c) Strong organizational, time management, communication, and interpersonal skills are essential, along with the ability to work independently and collaboratively; (d) Proficiency in office software like Excel and PowerPoint is required, and familiarity with design tools, AI platforms, social media, and event management software is an advantage; (e) Candidates must demonstrate fluency in written and spoken English and Chinese (Mandarin and Cantonese). Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Administrative Assistant, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/96/HL/AA) Duties The appointee is responsible for: (i) providing administrative and clerical support to the School; (ii) preparing for meetings, reports, seminars, and presentation materials; (iii) answering enquiries; (iv) assisting in the School's functions/ activities; and (v) undertaking such other duties as determined by the Dean or other reporting officers. Appointment Criteria Applicants should: (i) have a recognised Bachelor's degree; (ii) be competent in computing applications; (iii) have good communication skills and fluency in English and Chinese; and (iv) be a good team player with a strong sense of responsibility. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Choir Accompanist, Saint Francis University Choir (Ref.: 26/95/CHOIR/ACCOMPANIST) Duties Provide musical support and guidance to other performers; Rehearsal and practice with performers; Assist with stage and equipment setup with appropriate sound. Appointment Criteria A bachelor's degree in music, with a specialization in Piano Performance or Accompaniment; At least 3 years of solid experience in demonstration of musical performance; Experience accompanying choirs or vocalists; A collaborative and flexible approach to music-making with high adaptability to various musical styles. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Vocal Coach, Saint Francis University Choir (Ref.: 26/94/CHOIR/COACH) Duties Support the Conductor in all aspects of choir rehearsals especial in singing technique and voice development; Collaborate with the choir conductor in selecting repertoire and designing performance programmes; Coordinate logistics for rehearsals, performances, and other related activities; Provide guidance and feedback to choir members with mentorship. Appointment Criteria A bachelor's degree in music with specialization in vocal studies; At least 3 years of solid experience in demonstration of musical performance and experience as a vocal coach; Good musicianship and knowledge of choral repertoire across various styles and periods; A good team player with good interpersonal skills and supportive character. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Conductor, Saint Francis University Choir (Ref.: 26/93/CHOIR/CONDUCTOR) Duties Choir rehearsal and conduct musical performance in various university events and occasions and external performances; Guide and lead choir members in vocal technique, interpretation and musical expression with a supportive and inclusive environment to develop their musical abilities; Collaborate with other musicians and composers to create innovative and engaging musical programmes; Preferably, can provide artistic vision and leadership to enrich holistic education and spiritual life of campus community of Saint Francis University. Appointment Criteria At least 7 years of solid experience in demonstration of leadership skills as a Choir Conductor; Proven experience as a choral conductor, with a strong record of successful performances; Exceptional musicianship and knowledge of choral repertoire across various styles and periods; Strong leadership to inspire and motivate choir members; Ability to give clear instructions and make decisions under pressure; At least a Bachelor's degree (or higher) in Music, with a specialization in Choral Conducting or related discipline. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Manager (Finance), Finance & Estates Office (Ref.: 26/89/FEO/M) Duties Prepare annual budgets and long-term financial plans, ensure effective resources allocation. Oversee and manage project and school accounts, including income, expenditure, budgeting, and financial reporting, ensuring accuracy, completeness, and compliance with relevant policies and funding requirements. Monitor the status of the progress and financial status of projects and activities. Provide regular analyses and summaries to project owners and stakeholders. Implement and maintain robust financial and budgetary controls and monitoring mechanisms to ensure compliance with the established policies and procedures. Review and verify payments, invoices, and procurement documentation to ensure accuracy and compliance. Monitor income streams, ensuring accurate recording, timely recognition, and proper allocation of funds in accordance with approved budgets and funding agreements. Track income receipts against funding schedules and follow up on outstanding receivables to ensure timely collection. Ensure compliance with accounting standards, statutory requirements, and internal audit requirements in relation to project accounts. Contribute to the development and enhancement of financial policies, procedures, and systems. Prepare accurate and timely financial and management reports, forecast, variance analyses, and other relevant information. Undertake ad hoc assignments and special projects as required by supervisors. Appointment Criteria Applicants should possess the following criteria: A recognized bachelor's degree or above level in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a related discipline; A professional accounting qualification (e.g. HKCPA); At least 5 years of relevant post-qualification experience in accounting or financial management, preferably within higher education, the public sector or large organisations; Strong knowledge of financial management, budgeting, accounting standards and procurement practices; Experience in handling project accounts and financial monitoring; Good analytical skills with the ability to interpret financial data and identity key issues; Strong attention to detail and high level of accuracy in financial work; and Good communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with internal and external stakeholders. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Public Affairs Officer (Marketing), Public Affairs Office (Ref.: 26/88/PAO/O) Duties The Public Affairs Office (PAO) is seeking a creative and digitally savvy individual to support its marketing and communications initiatives. Reporting to the Assistant Director of Public Affairs, the appointee will be primarily responsible for: Executing social media and content marketing initiatives to enhance the University's digital presence, drive engagement, and support broader branding and marketing objectives; Creating high-quality written, visual, and multimedia content for online and offline platforms, and managing digital and social media channels such as LinkedIn, Instagram, WeChat, RedNote, and Facebook; Producing high quality marketing collateral, event and promotional materials; Attending events and activities to capture content, including photography, video, and real-time social media updates, for promotional use; Work closely with internal teams and stakeholders to ensure content and campaigns are aligned with the University's branding, messaging, and communication priorities; Coordinating with external service providers for digital campaigns, targeted advertising, SEO/ SEM, and social media support; Supporting the University's offline branding and marketing events and activities; and Performing any other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria A recognised degree, preferably in Marketing, Communications, Journalism, Public Relations, Multimedia, Digital Media, Design, or a related discipline; 3–5 years of relevant experience in digital marketing, content creation, social media management, or integrated marketing communications; Solid experience in creating written, visual, and multimedia content for digital and social media platforms; Strong practical skills in online and offline production, including copywriting, graphic design, photography, video shooting, and video editing; Proficiency in relevant creative and editing tools, such as Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, Premiere Pro, Canva, CapCut, or equivalent applications; Sound knowledge of major social media platforms and their content requirements, including LinkedIn, Instagram, WeChat, RedNote, and Facebook; Good knowledge of SEO, SEM, digital campaigns, social media promotions, and paid media execution, with relevant hands-on experience being an advantage. Good understanding of branding, digital engagement, and online content trends, with an eye for visual presentation and audience appeal; Strong command of written and spoken English and Chinese; Good organisational and project coordination skills, with the ability to manage multiple tasks and meet tight deadlines; A proactive, detail-minded, and responsible team player with good interpersonal and communication skills; and Flexible and willing to work outside office hours when necessary. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Manager (Marketing), Public Affairs Office (Ref.: 26/87/PAO/M) Duties The Public Affairs Office (PAO) is seeking a seasoned individual to support its marketing and communications initiatives. Reporting to the Assistant Director of Public Affairs, the appointee will be primarily responsible for: Driving the development of branding and marketing strategies, and overseeing integrated full-funnel campaigns to strengthen the University's visibility and market positioning; Planning and delivering data-informed digital marketing campaigns across multiple channels, including the University website, paid search, paid social, display advertising, and content marketing; Developing organic content (including social media posts, visuals, photography, and videos) and managing official social media platforms such as Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, WeChat and RedNote to drive branding and student recruitment efforts; Working closely with internal stakeholders, external agencies, and partners to implement promotional initiatives and achieve defined KPIs; Driving performance monitoring and analytics, including website traffic, campaign effectiveness, and competitor benchmarking, and providing strategic insights and recommendations to inform continuous improvement; Supporting the University's offline branding and marketing events and activities; Monitoring social media trends, platform developments, and online community sentiment, and supporting the identification and mitigation of potential reputational risks in collaboration with the communication team; and Performing any other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria A recognised degree, preferably in Marketing, Business, Journalism, Communications, Public Relations, or a related discipline; 8 -15 years of solid experience in branding and digital marketing, with a proven track record in social media strategy, content development, performance marketing, analytics, and lead generation; Demonstrated success in developing and driving integrated, omni-channel marketing strategies, including SEO/ SEM, social media growth, paid advertising, and delivering measurable outcomes; Strong practical knowledge of key digital platforms and Martech tools, including Google Ads, Google Analytics, Meta Ads, and related solutions; A strategic and analytical mindset, with the ability to interpret complex data, derive insights, and translate them into effective marketing strategies and business impact; Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese; proficiency in Putonghua is an advantage; Hands-on skills in design and video production tools (e.g. Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, Premiere Pro or equivalent) would be an advantage; A mature, self-driven professional with strong sense of ownership, attention to detail, and a solutions-oriented approach; Proven ability to lead and collaborate effectively within small, agile teams, with strong interpersonal and stakeholder management skills; Highly organised, with strong project management, prioritisation, and time management capabilities; Ability to manage multiple initiatives independently in a fast-paced environment, while maintaining quality under tight timelines; and Flexible and willing to work outside office hours when necessary. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Assistant Manager (Marketing), Public Affairs Office (Ref.: 26/86/PAO/AM) Duties The Public Affairs Office (PAO) is seeking a dynamic individual to support its marketing and communications initiatives. Reporting to the Assistant Director of Public Affairs, the appointee will be primarily responsible for: Supporting the development of branding and marketing strategies, and executing integrated full-funnel campaigns to strengthen the University's visibility and market positioning; Planning and implementing data-informed digital marketing campaigns across multiple channels, including the University website, paid search, paid social, display advertising, and content marketing; Creating and managing organic content (including social media posts, visuals, photography, and videos) and overseeing official social media platforms such as Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, WeChat and RedNote to support branding and student recruitment; Coordinating with internal stakeholders, external agencies, and partners to deliver promotional initiatives and achieve defined KPIs; Monitoring and analysing campaign performance, including website traffic, campaign effectiveness, and competitor activities, and preparing regular reports with actionable recommendations; Supporting the delivery of offline branding and marketing events and activities; and Performing any other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria A recognised degree, preferably in Marketing, Business, Journalism, Communications, Public Relations, or a related discipline; 5–8 years of relevant experience in branding and digital marketing, with a proven track record in social media strategy, content development, performance marketing, analytics, and lead generation; Demonstrated experience in executing integrated, omni-channel marketing strategies, including SEO/ SEM, social media growth, paid advertising, and delivering measurable outcomes; Solid practical knowledge of key digital platforms and Martech tools, including Google Ads, Google Analytics, Meta Ads, and related solutions; Analytical mindset with the ability to interpret data, derive insights, and translate them into effective marketing actions; Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese; proficiency in Putonghua is an advantage; Hands-on skills in design and video production tools (e.g., Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, Premiere Pro or equivalent) would be an advantage; A mature, self-driven professional with strong sense of ownership, attention to detail, and a solutions-oriented approach; Ability to work effectively within a small, agile team, with good interpersonal and communication skills; Well-organised, with strong project management, prioritisation, and time management capabilities; Capable of managing multiple tasks independently in a fast-paced environment while meeting tight deadlines; and Flexible and willing to work outside office hours when necessary. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Administrative Officer (Scholarship Program), Student Affairs Office (Ref.: 26/83/SAO/AO) Duties Develop and implement strategies to promote scholarship opportunities to the student body. Collaborate with academic departments to identify and nominate qualified candidates. Maintain and update a comprehensive database of scholarship recipients. Liaise with the University Advancement Office to align scholarship administration with donor expectations and agreements. Coordinate all aspects of the scholarship selection process, including panel interviews. Plan and execute the annual Scholarship Thanksgiving Reception for donors and recipients. Organize selection panels and preparatory training for students entering external scholarship competitions. Appointment Criteria A good honours degree, with relevant working experience preferably in higher education or community services. Possession of postgraduate qualification would be an advantage. Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua), working knowledge of computer applications, dynamic personality and tactful communication with different sectors of personnel are required. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Assistant Manager, Registry (Ref.: 26/82/REG/AM) Duties The appointee is responsible for (a) managing the administrative arrangements relating to student admission, registration, enrolment, timetabling, assessment, graduation as well as record keeping of students and academic staff members of both Institutions; (b) managing the implementation of the administrative quality assurance process in the registrarial services; and (c) contributing to the development, implementation and improvement of the management support system; (d) contributing in the overall production of Registry-related publications; and (e) improving the above functions by using the technologies. Appointment Criteria Applicants should (a) possess a recognized degree with at least 5 years' post-qualification administrative experience (experience in the Registry related discipline will be given preference); (b) proficiency in MS Office programs; (c) outstanding communication skills with excellent command of both written and spoken English and Chinese; and (d) proven ability to work independently with effective teamwork skills, self-motivated and able to work under pressure. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Administrative Officer, Student Affairs Office (Ref.: 26/79/SAO/AO) Duties The key responsibilities of the Administrative Officer (Central Admin) are: Serving as the departmental coordinator for procurement and PR processing for the SAO; Managing the staff roster for the SAO enquiry hotline and ensuring the smooth operation of counter services; Co-ordinating with teams to publish student stories and achievements, creating and uploading digital content to the SAO website, and managing direct communications with relevant stakeholders; Organize campus wide student cultural & music programs; Acting as the co-ordinator for the working group on U-Life Orientation Day; Overseeing the departmental assets database; and Co-ordinating with the GE office to develop a list of endorsed service activities for students to meet community service requirements. Appointment Criteria A recognised bachelor's degree; At least 3 years experience in an administrative role in business or education environment; Strong organizational and project management skills with attention to details; Ability to work under pressure and meet multiple deadlines; Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information with discretion and professionalism; Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook); and Good command of both written and spoken English, Mandarin and Cantonese. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Administrative Officer, Graduate School (Ref.: 26/73/GS/AO) Duties The appointee will be responsible for (i) providing administrative support for the programme accreditation;(ii) serving as secretary to various committees of Graduate School; (iii) drafting and preparing documents of Graduate School; (iv) undertaking such other duties as determined by the Dean of Graduate Studies. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognised Bachelor's degree; (b) a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); (c) proficiency in computer applications; (d) good organisational and communication skills; and (e) relevant work experience. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Administrative Officer, Centre for Applied Ethics (Ref.: 26/68/CAE/AO) Duties Provide administrative support in daily operation and development of the Centre for Applied Ethics; Assist in the implementation of the Centre for Applied Ethics' functions and cross functions; Conduct comprehensive data collection and analysis for project proposals and evaluation; Handle logistics arrangements, including materials preparation, participant coordination, and on-site support for various events and activities; Liaise with internal and external stakeholders, vendors, and service providers to ensure smooth operations; Handle incoming and outgoing correspondence, including emails, letters, and phone calls; Undertake other duties as assigned by supervisor(s). Appointment Criteria A recognized bachelor's degree is required; a master's degree is an advantage; Good organizational and project management skills with attention to details; Ability to work under pressure and meet multiple deadlines; Good command of design and AI tool is a plus; Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook); and Good command of written and spoken English, Chinese and Putonghua. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Manager (Infrastructure Support), Information Technology Services Centre (Ref.: 26/62/ITSC/M) Duties The appointee will be responsible for assisting the Director, ITSC, for managing the day-to-day operations of the Information Technology Services Centre (ITSC): (i) managing and delivering infrastructure ensuring sound architecture, reliability, technology and function across network, servers, storage, database, application platform and end user equipment; (ii) providing end user help desk and support services on all IT services; (iii) providing on-call support to ensure systems availability in accordance to target service level; (iv) directing, implementing and overseeing standard IT practices, which include: Computer Operations, Backups, Information Security Safeguards, System and Network Monitoring, Infrastructure Upgrades and Enhancements; (v) liaising with vendors to deliver various IT projects; and (vi) undertaking such other duties as assigned by supervisors. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have: (i) a recognised postgraduate degree in Computer Science, Information Technology or related disciplines; (ii) at least 10 years' relevant experience, preferably in a similar position in local/ overseas higher education institutions; (iii) sound technical background, a generalist of IT technologies and also a specialist on core technologies; (iv) strong team and vendor management; (v) good communication and problem solving skills; and (vi) a good command of spoken and written English and Chinese. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Administrative Officer, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences  (Ref.: 26/60/HS/AO) Duties The appointee will be responsible for Provide comprehensive administrative support for programme operation; Liaise effectively with internal and external parties; Provide support for committee meetings; Manage multiple tasks efficiently with strong prioritization, reliability, and attention to detail; Provide support for School events and projects; Perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences or his delegates. Appointment Criteria Applicants for the above position should A relevant recognized Bachelor's degree with at least 2 years' relevant work experience; Detail-minded and able to work as a team and work independently; Good organizational and time management skills; Good communication and interpersonal abilities; Proficient in project and event management tools; Strong data analysis skills, with the ability to optimize project outcomes; and Proficient in using office software, such as Excel, PowerPoint, etc. Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Mandarin and Cantonese). Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Administrative Officer, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref.: 26/52/SS/AO) Duties The appointee will be responsible for (i) drafting and preparing discussion papers, proposals, correspondences and reports; (ii) serving as secretary to such committees as assigned; (iii) providing administrative support for teaching and learning; institutional review, programme validation, revalidation and accreditation; (iv) coordinating a team for administrative duties; (v) assisting in the two Institutions' functions; and (vi) undertaking such other duties as determined by the Supervisors. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognised Bachelor's degree; (b) a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); (c) proficiency in computer applications; (d) good organisational and communication skills; and (e) relevant work experience. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Programme Officer (Multicultural Care and Service Learning Project), Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref.: 26/51/SS/PO) Duties The appointee will assist the Project Fund Holder in the coordination and implementation of the Multicultural Care and Service-Learning Project, including: (i) supporting the planning and delivery of training and service-learning programmes; (ii) coordinating with collaborating schools, NGOs and community partners; (iii) assisting in meetings, programme administration, and placement coordination; (iv) preparing operational documents, reports and project records; (v) supporting programme monitoring, data collection and evaluation activities; and (vi) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) Higher Diploma in Social Sciences or related discipline, or equivalent qualification; (ii) preferably Registered Social Worker, with knowledge of or experience working with Ethnically Diverse (ED) population; (iii) good command of English and Chinese; with proficiency in ED languages an advantage, and (iv) Good organizational and interpersonal skills with cultural sensitivity. The appointment will be for one year, renewable subject to availability of funding. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Administrative Officer (Finance), Finance and Estates Office (Ref.: 26/47/FEO/AO) Duties The appointee will be attached to the Finance and Estates Office of the University and will assist with the following duties: Preparing analyses for budgeting and management accounting purposes; Processing transactions onto the Financial Management Information System; Managing accounts for government-funded and/ or non-government funded projects, including account setup, monitoring and reporting, ensure compliance with funders' regulations/ requirements and the University's financial management policies; Preparing various reports and returns for submission to the Education Bureau and/ or other Government departments; and Carrying out ad hoc administration work as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognised degree (preferably in business administration or accounting disciplines); (b) a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; (c) proficiency in computer applications; and (d) good analytical, organizing and communication skills. Preference will be given to applicants with hands-on experience in budget preparation and financial/ management accounting in NGOs or education sector. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Administrative Officer, University Secretariat (Ref.: 26/46/US/AO) Duties Provide administrative support in organising university activities, staff events, and training workshops; occasional day trips may be required; Design posters, promotional materials, and other event-related artwork; Handle logistics arrangements, including materials preparation, participant coordination, and on-site support for various events and activities; Liaise with internal and external stakeholders, vendors, and service providers to ensure smooth operations; Handle incoming and outgoing correspondence, including emails, letters, and phone calls; Provide general administrative support to the University Secretariat and Chaplaincy; Perform other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria A recognised bachelor's degree; Proven experience in administration, preferably in a fast-paced environment; Strong organizational and project management skills with attention to details; Ability to work under pressure and meet multiple deadlines; Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information with discretion and professionalism; Good command of design and AI tool; Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook); and Good command of both written and spoken English, Mandarin and Cantonese. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled (3 months/ 5months) Temporary Executive Assistant, Registry (Ref.: 26/41&42/REG/EA/TEMP) Appointment period: 26/41/REG/EA/TEMP : June to August 2026 (3 months) or negotiable 26/42/REG/EA/TEMP : June to October 2026 (5 months) or negotiable Duties The appointee is responsible for (a) providing administrative and clerical support in the Registry; (b) performing counter duties; (c) answering enquiries; (d) assisting with functions/ activities; (e) managing storage; and (f) undertaking other duties as assigned by the Registrar, Assistant Registrars, or other reporting officers. Working outside normal office hours may be required occasionally. Appointment Criteria Applicants for the post of Executive Assistant II should (a) hold a sub-degree qualification or be currently studying for a Higher Diploma/ Associate Degree/ Degree in any discipline; (b) have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); (c) be competent in computing application, (d) possess good communication skills with a pleasant, polite, and friendly personality; (e) be a good team player with a strong sense of responsibility; and (f) have 1 year's relevant work experience (preferable). Candidates with more experience may be considered for the post of Executive Assistant I. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Assistant Manager (Student Recruitment and Engagement Team), Public Affairs Office (Ref.: 26/36/PAO/AM) Duties The successful candidate will be responsible for implementing strategic initiatives to enhance the School's engagement with external stakeholders, including feeder schools, prospective students, alumni, university partners, and the broader community. The appointee will support the Assistant Director, Recruitment and Engagement at the Public Affairs Office in leading admissions and partnership development for the local market. The appointee will lead recruitment and partnership initiatives to strengthen collaboration between the University and Hong Kong Secondary Schools, including organising information sessions for principals and teachers, conducting school visits to enhance recruitment, and hosting networking events for external stakeholders. The appointee will also build and maintain strong relationships with targeted feeder schools and partner organisations to expand the School's network and influence, and will identify and pursue strategic partnership opportunities, such as drafting and managing Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs). This is a KPI driven role. The role also includes planning and overseeing events such as conferences, exchange programmes, and stakeholder engagement activities. Key responsibilities: Support the development and implementation of external relations and stakeholder engagement plans to enhance the School's reputation and increase student recruitment. Identify and build relationships with key stakeholders, including secondary schools in Hong Kong, prospective students, alumni, university partners, and government authorities. Assist in planning, executing, and coordinating stakeholder engagement events and activities, such as conferences, ceremonies, and visits. Devise and implement stakeholder engagement plans to strengthen stakeholder relations, foster a close-knit SFU community, and support the ongoing expansion of the SFU profile other duties as assigned by the Assistant Director (Recruitment and Engagement). Appointment Criteria Applicants must possess a bachelor's degree, preferably in a business-related discipline, and have at least three years of relevant post-qualification experience in a higher education institution. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong problem-solving abilities, an outgoing disposition, the capacity to work independently and collaboratively, meticulous attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple tasks under strict deadlines. Candidates should be self-motivated, effective team players, and exhibit strong interpersonal, communication, and coordination skills. Proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese is essential. Occasional work outside regular office hours, including weekends, public holidays, or evenings, may be required. The appointment is for one year, with the possibility of renewal. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Full-time/ Part-time Laboratory Technician, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/13/HS/LT) Duties Provide support for teaching, research and service to the School of Health Sciences in the nursing and other health-care courses. Follow school directions for nursing skills laboratory station set-up and aftercare of supplies/equipment in all teaching, skills assessment and students' self-practice Assist in the setting up, operation and maintenance of the equipment required for teaching / learning activities including manikins, simulation models, patient-care equipment and other computing / audio visual facilities. Maintain inventory of laboratory equipment and supplies to ensure equipment are in good condition and supplies are adequate. Maintain the daily operation of the nursing skills laboratories and ensure a safe and clean condition in all work areas. Assist in-house and vendor servicing of laboratory equipment, follow any required repairs / maintenance and to keep updated records for tracking. Support and facilitate the student self-practice sessions in the nursing skills laboratories. Perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of the School of Health Sciences or his delegates. The appointee may be required to work outside normal office hours and on Saturdays and Sundays due to specific operational requirement. Appointment Criteria Five passes in HKCEE/HKDSE including English Language, Chinese Language and Mathematics. Good computer knowledge and experience in using application software such as MS Office, photo/video editing software and e-learning system, etc. Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese. Good communication, interpersonal and organizational skills; and able to work independently. Preferred Attributes / Exposure Working experience in health care institution Holding certificate of health care related study Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Administrative Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/07/HS/AA) Duties The appointee will be responsible for Providing administrative support to academic programmes and general office management; Assist in organising departmental events, student activities and academic visits; Compile records and maintain databases; Handle enquiries from students and external parties; and Performing other tasks as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have Achieved Level 2 or above in five subjects in the HKDSE, or have obtained Grade E or above in five subjects in the HKCEE; Proficiency in MS Office, including Word and Excel; A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; Good organisational and communication skills; and Preferably with 1-2 year's relevant work experience. Those with lower qualifications may be considered for the post of Administrative Assistant II. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled"
    },
    "https://www.sfu.edu.hk/en/career/research-project-positions/index.html": {
      "title": "Research / Project Positions",
      "description": "Saint Francis University - Research / Project Positions Research / Project Positions Notes For Applicants: Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested parties are invited to submit: a written application indicating expected salary; a CV; and a duly completed application form Please email to hrm@sfu.edu.hk before the application deadline. Candidates not invited for interview within 2 months after the application deadline may assume their applications unsuccessful. Download Application Form here All personal data provided by the applicants will be treated in strict confidence and used only for recruitment and employment-related purposes. Research / Project Positions Research Assistant, Yam Pak Charitable Foundation School of Computing and Information Sciences (Ref.: 26/124/CIS/RA) The University invites applications for a research position on an RGC-funded collaborative project that develops an AIoT structural health monitoring and early-warning system for construction tower cranes. The project combines a \"Digital Triple\" methodology — a scaled physical prototype governed by dynamic similarity, finite element modelling, and physics-informed AI digital twins — with wireless sensor networks, edge computing, and deep learning (1D-DCNN / LSTM) to detect structural fatigue and damage and to predict and prevent crane instability and collapse. The appointee will join a multidisciplinary team of engineers and data scientists, work with real instrumented crane structures and laboratory prototypes, and contribute to publishable research outputs of direct relevance to construction safety in Hong Kong. Duties The appointee will assist the Principal Investigator and Co-Investigators in: designing, assembling and calibrating IoT sensor nodes (MEMS accelerometers, strain gauges, inclinometers, anemometers, GNSS/IMU units) and their wireless data-acquisition and edge-computing hardware; deploying and maintaining monitoring instrumentation on laboratory crane prototypes and on-site tower cranes, including wiring, power, communications and enclosure work; developing embedded firmware and data pipelines for real-time acquisition, transmission, storage and visualisation of vibration and structural response data; and performing other project-related duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have: an honours degree in Electronic Engineering, Mechatronic Engineering, Electrical and Electronic Engineering, or a closely related discipline (a Master's/MPhil degree will be an advantage); practical experience with embedded systems, microcontrollers and sensors (e.g. Arduino, ESP32, Raspberry Pi, STM32), sensor interfacing and IoT communication protocols (Wi-Fi, LoRa, MQTT, 4G/5G); competence in signal processing and data analysis using Python and/or MATLAB; the ability to work independently, carry out laboratory and field work, and troubleshoot hardware and software problems systematically; and a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese), with strong technical report-writing skills. Preference will be given to candidates with experience in structural health monitoring, vibration measurement, edge AI, digital twins, or construction-related instrumentation. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Senior Research Assistant, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref.: 26/115/SS/RA) Duties The appointee will assist the Principal Investigator and Co-Principal Investigators under Caregiving Research and Development Centre. His/her task will include (i) assisting in the preparation of research proposals, funding applications, ethics submissions and project reports; (ii) conducting literature reviews, designing research instruments and coordinating research projects; (iii) conducting qualitative and quantitative data collection and analysis using software such as NVivo and SPSS; (iv) arranging and conducting interviews and focus groups, as well as designing survey questionnaires; (v) drafting research manuscripts and presentation materials for conferences and journals; (vi) assisting in the development of operational manuals, training materials and reports; (vii) supporting event planning and project-related activities; and (viii) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) a Bachelor's degree, preferably with a Master's/MPhil degree in Social Sciences or a related discipline; (ii) solid training and experience in research methods and data analysis, both quantitative and qualitative; (iii) demonstrated experience in preparing research proposals, funding applications, research reports and academic manuscripts; (iv) excellent English and Chinese proficiency; (v) a minimum of two years of relevant experience in research project coordination, data analysis, research report writing and/or academic publication. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/114/HL/RA) Duties The appointee will assist in the research project on: (a) administrative and coordinating work (b) collecting data and pre-processing them for experiments; (c) recruiting participants in experiments; (d) annotating data; (e) managing and updating datasets; (f) preparing reports; and (g) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognized Bachelor's degree in humanities field; (b) solid research experience; (c) excellent communication and interpersonal skills; (d) positive attitude and ability to work well in a team; (e) proficiency in both written and spoken Chinese and English; and (f) proficiency in computer applications. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/110/HS/RA) Duties The appointee will support the Principal Investigator in a research project aimed at \"Development and evaluation of a Chatbot to Enhance Clinical Learning in Nursing Students\". The appointee will be responsible to assist administrative and coordinating work for the research project. Tasks include: (a) arranging the research study; (b) collecting data and conducting data analysis; (c) preparing reports; (d) organizing seminars and workshops; (d) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should (i) have a recognised Bachelor's Degree; (ii) have relevant research experience in the handling of data entry, transcription and utilizing SPSS software analysis; (iii) be able to work independently, attention to detail with positive working attitude; and (iv) have good communication skills and fluency in English and Chinese. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref.: 26/101/SS/RA) Duties The appointee will assist the Principal Investigator (PI) in a research project aimed how capitals affect students' engagement with GenAI tools and their academic performance on: (a) review and conduct literature review; (b) recruiting participants; (c) perform quantitative data analysis (d) prepare materials for conference presentations and publications; (e) handle relevant administrative tasks; (f) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognized bachelor's degree or above in social sciences or a related discipline, preferably in the area of Psychology and/or Sociology; (b) solid research experience; (c) excellent communication and interpersonal skills; (d) positive attitude, responsible, self-motivated and ability to work independently; (e) proficiency in both written and spoken English; (f) proficiency in using analytical tools (e.g., SPSS or R). Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Senior Research Assistant, Graduate School (Ref.: 26/100/GS/RA) Duties The appointee is mainly required to assist in an innovative research project entitled ' An Integrative Psychosocial Study and Service Outcome Evaluation for Students with Special Educational Needs . The appointee will assist the Principal Investigator, the Co-investigators and the team in conducting the research tasks, including: (a) reviewing literature; (b) conducting large-scale mixed-method research; (c) coordinating with research team members and collaborating partners; (d) collecting and analyzing quantitative and qualitative data; (e) conducting in-depth interviews; (f) compiling research reports and high-impact peer-reviewed journal articles; (g) supervising research assistants, and (h) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants for Senior Research Assistant should (i) have a recognised Master's degree or above in Social Sciences / Applied Psychology / Statistics / Computer or Data Science; (ii) with at least five years of relevant research experience in quantitative and qualitative research methods, a track record of publications will be considered an advantage; (iii) familiar with procedures of research adopting randomized controlled trial and/or mixed-methods; (iv) have knowledge in data analytic software, including SPSS and NVivo, knowledge in Statistical modeling will be considered an advantage; (v) able to work independently, have an investigative nature and an analytical aptitude, attention to detail, ability to synthesize research into clear, compelling outputs; and (vi) have good communication skills and fluency in English and Chinese. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences  (Ref.: 26/99/HS/RA) Duties The appointee will support a project that aims to explore nurses' perspectives on promoting advanced directives and assess their capacity to manage end-of-life care and related issues. Responsibilities include (a) coordinating activities, (b) collecting and analyzing both quantitative and qualitative data, (c) reviewing the relevant literature, (d) providing administrative support, (e) assisting the research team in preparing research reports, and (f) performing any other duties assigned by the project leader. Appointment Criteria Applicants must meet the following criteria: (i) possess a recognized Master's degree in statistics, health sciences, or a related field; (ii) have at five years of relevant post-qualification experience; (iii) demonstrate a strong command of both written and spoken Chinese and English; and (iv) exhibit proficiency in SPSS, along with experience in both quantitative and qualitative data collection and analysis. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Full-time / Part-time Research Assistant, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref.: 26/97/SS/RA) Duties The appointee will support the Principal Investigator in a research project aimed at collecting data from South Asian communities. Irregular working hours and/or weekend work may be required, particularly for data collection The appointee will be responsible to: conduct literature review; recruit research participants and conduct in-depth interviews; perform qualitative data analysis and compile research reports; prepare materials for conference presentations and publications; handle relevant administrative tasks; perform other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should: have a recognized bachelor degree or above in social sciences or relevant disciplines; have at least one year of relevant work experience; have a good network within South Asian communities; be familiar with procedures for conducting in-depth interviews; possess knowledge and skills in qualitative data analysis; have good communication, organizational and interpersonal skills; be responsible, self-motivated and able to work independently; have an excellent command of both written and spoken English and Chinese. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/91/HS/RA) Duties The appointee will be responsible to assist staff members within the School to conduct administrative and coordinating research activities and research projects. Tasks include: (a) literature search, (b) coordinating research work, (c) collecting data and conducting data analysis; (d) preparing reports; and (e) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) at least a bachelor's degree in nursing, health science, allied health backgrounds, or statistics-related qualifications; (ii) 3-4 years of research experience and knowledge of quantitative research, and prior experience of conducting statistical analysis are preferred. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Project Officer, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/85/HL/PO) Duties The appointees will (a) assist the work of system construction and maintenance of the project; (b) help with the teaching of computer-related courses of the programmes of the School; and (c) perform other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a bachelor's degree or master's degree in computer science or relevant fields; (b) familiarity with database management tools (such as SQL, MS Access, etc.); (c) knowledge and skills of programming (such as Python); (d) proficiency in image technology; and (e) able to work independently. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, Yam Pak Charitable Foundation School of Computing and Information Sciences (Ref.: 26/84/CIS/RA) We are seeking a self-motivated, capable, and research-oriented individual to join our team as a Research Assistant for the RGC-funded project: \"Harnessing Large Language Models for Social Trust: Automated Fact-checking for Public Health Informatics by Large Language Models\" Project No.: UGC/FDS11/E05/25 This position is particularly suitable for applicants who wish to strengthen their research profile, gain hands-on experience in AI and large language model (LLM) applications, and contribute to publishable research outputs. The project focuses on the application of LLMs to automated fact-checking, public health informatics, misinformation detection, and social trust. Applicants with relevant experience or a strong interest in LLMs, AI applications, NLP, data analytics, or research publication are highly encouraged to apply. Duties The appointee will be responsible for supporting the project team in conducting research related to LLMs. Major duties include assisting in literature review, data collection and analysis, experiment design and implementation, result interpretation, manuscript preparation, and publication of research findings in scientific journals and conferences. The appointee is also expected to complete other research-related tasks assigned by the Project Leader. Appointment Criteria Applicants should possess: A Bachelor's Degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Information Technology, or a related discipline; The ability to work independently and responsibly; Good communication and interpersonal skills; Good English writing skills; and A strong interest in research, AI, LLMs, NLP, or data-driven applications. Applicants with prior research experience, publication experience, programming skills, or hands-on experience with LLMs will be given priority. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filledl Part-time Research Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/80/HS/RA) Duties The appointee will assist in the research project on \"Mental health literacy, psychological well-being and healthy ageing perceptions of community-based older adults with low to mild distress in Hong Kong: A mixed methods study\". The appointee will assist the Principal Investigator in: Recruitment of research participants from the community; Obtaining consent documents and data collection including administering surveys; Conducting semi-structured interviews and transcribing audio recordings; Performing basic quantitative data analysis using SPSS and preliminary qualitative thematic analysis; Working mainly in SFU and visiting NGO centres (if required); and Performing any other duties as assigned by PI. Appointment Criteria A recognized bachelor's degree or above in Nursing, health science or a related discipline; 1-2 years of research experience and knowledge of quantitative and qualitative research; Prior experience of conducting statistical analysis and thematic analysis; Have a good interpersonal and communication skills; and Be able to work independently. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/77/HL/RA) Duties The appointee will assist in the research project \" The Importance of Disciplinary Literacy in iGCSE: A Data Driven Study in Hong Kong \" on: (a) administrative and coordinating work (b) collecting data and pre-processing them for data analysis; (c) recruiting school participants; (d) annotating data; (e) managing and updating datasets; (f) preparing reports; and (g) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognized Bachelor's degree in humanities field, preferably in the area of English language education and/or linguistics; (b) solid research experience; (c) excellent communication and interpersonal skills; (d) positive attitude and ability to work well in a team; (e) proficiency in both written and spoken English;  (f) proficiency in computer applications; and (g) corpus knowledge is preferable. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, Graduate School (Ref.: 26/76/GS/RA) Duties The appointee is mainly required to assist in a 5-year innovative service-research project entitled 'Meta-S: An Integrative Psychosocial Study and Service Outcome Evaluation for Students with Special Educational Needs'. The appointee will assist the Principal Investigator, the Co-investigators, and the team in carrying out project-related tasks, including: (a) supporting the planning and coordination of project activities (e.g. seminars, workshops); (b) arranging and conducting research activities (e.g. surveys, in-depth interviews); (c) preparing and analyzing data derived from the project; (d) compiling research reports and publication; (e) handling relevant administrative tasks, and (f) performing other duties as assigned by the PI. Appointment Criteria Applicants should (i) have a recognized Bachelor's degree or above in Social Work / Social Sciences / Education / Applied Research / Applied Psychology / Statistics; (ii) have relevant project or event management / research experience; (iii) have knowledge of Special Educational Needs (SEN) / Neurodiversity (ND); (iv) be able to work independently, have an investigative nature, attention to detail, and an analytical aptitude; (v) have good teamwork and interpersonal skills; and (vi) have good communication skills and fluency in English and Chinese. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref.: 26/72/SS/RA) Duties The appointee will assist the Principal Investigator in all research related activities, include arranging and conducting survey questionnaires, interviews & focus groups with parents; conducting data analysis of the quantitative data and qualitative verbatim transcription; assisting in drafting operational manuals, forms, templates and reports; drafting research manuscripts for presentation/publication in conferences/journals; performing other tasks as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) a Bachelor's degree, preferably with a Master's/MPhil degree in Social Sciences or a related discipline; (ii) solid training and experience in research methods, using SPSS software; (iii) excellent English and Chinese proficiency Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, School of Computing and Information Sciences (Ref.: 26/67/CIS/RA) Join a cutting-edge research initiative at Saint Francis University. The project, \"AI and IoT in Telehealth,\" lies at the intersection of modern healthcare and technological innovation. We aim to leverage Internet of Things (IoT) medical devices and Artificial Intelligence (AI) to revolutionize remote patient monitoring, improve clinical decision-making, and bridge the gap in accessible healthcare. We are seeking a driven, multidisciplinary Full-Time Research Assistant to bridge the gap between health sciences and advanced technology. You will play a pivotal role in designing, testing, and implementing AI-driven telehealth solutions and managing IoT data pipelines. Duties The appointee will be responsible (a) assist in the development, training, and deployment of AI/Machine Learning models tailored for healthcare data; (b) support the integration and testing of IoT biosensors and remote monitoring devices; (c) collect, clean, and analyze clinical and health-related datasets; (d) collaborate with clinical partners to ensure technical solutions align with real-world healthcare needs; (e) contribute to academic papers, research reports, and grant proposals; and (f) manage day-to-day project logistics and documentation. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) a Bachelor's or Master's degree in a Health Science-related field (e.g., Biomedical Science, Health Informatics, Nursing, Public Health) with a strong quantitative background, OR a degree in Biomedical Engineering / Computer Science with a heavy emphasis on healthcare applications; (ii) strong programming skills in Python or R (experience with frameworks like PyTorch, TensorFlow, or Scikit-learn is highly preferred); (iii) solid understanding of Machine Learning, Deep Learning, or statistical modeling techniques; (iv) familiarity with IoT concepts, data acquisition, or sensor technology; (v) excellent written and verbal communication skills for cross-disciplinary collaboration (tech and health); (vi) prior experience in a research environment or writing academic literature; and (vii) strong problem-solving skills and a passion for digital health innovation. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, School of Computing and Information Sciences (Ref.: 26/66/CIS/RA) Join an innovative, high-impact research initiative at Saint Francis University. The project, \"AI and IoT Monitoring of Construction Tower Cranes,\" focuses on enhancing smart city infrastructure and construction safety. By integrating Internet of Things (IoT) sensors with advanced Artificial Intelligence (AI), this project aims to enable real-time structural health monitoring, predictive maintenance, and anomaly detection for tower cranes on active construction sites. We are seeking a technically skilled, motivated Part-Time Research Assistant with an engineering background. In this role, you will help bridge the gap between structural/mechanical systems and intelligent data science, contributing directly to the deployment of IoT hardware and the development of AI algorithms. Duties The appointee will be responsible (a) develop, train, and test AI/Machine Learning models for anomaly detection and predictive analytics using sensor data; (b) assist in processing, cleaning, and managing time-series data streams from IoT sensors (e.g., accelerometers, strain gauges, tilt sensors); (c) support the configuration, calibration, and data acquisition setup for IoT monitoring hardware; (d) collaborate with the research team to validate AI model insights against real-world engineering constraints; and (e) assist in preparing technical reports, progress updates. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) a Bachelor's or Master's degree (or currently enrolled in a postgraduate program) in Engineering (e.g., Civil, Mechanical, Electronic, Systems, or Biomedical Engineering with a strong structural/mechatronics focus); (ii) strong programming skills in Python or MATLAB (experience with libraries like NumPy, Pandas, TensorFlow, or PyTorch is highly preferred); (iii) solid understanding of Machine Learning, Deep Learning, or statistical signal processing; (iv) ability to interpret data related to structural mechanics, vibrations, or kinematics; (v) experience working with IoT hardware, microcontrollers (e.g., Arduino, Raspberry Pi), or edge computing, (vi) strong problem-solving abilities and a self-driven attitude toward research; and (vii) good written and verbal communication skills. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences  (Ref.: 26/65/SS/RA) Duties The appointee will be responsible to: conduct literature review perform data analysis and compile research reports prepare materials for conference presentations and publications perform other duties as assigned Appointment Criteria Applicants should: have a recognized bachelor degree or above in data sciences or relevant disciplines with proficiency in SPSS / Python / LLM and other computer software possess strong knowledge and skills in data analysis for project evaluations have good communication, organizational and interpersonal skills be responsible, self-motivated and able to work independently have an excellent command of both written and spoken English and Chinese Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/64/HS/RA) Duties The appointee will play a key role in supporting a research project focused on \"Psychological\". Responsibilities include: Assisting in the management of the project; Coordinating with collaborative partners and project team; Providing support for the preparation of research material; Assisting in recruitment, data collection, data entry and data analysis; Conducting literature search; Assisting in the preparation of abstracts, manuscripts and reports; and Performing any other duties as assigned by the project leader or his/her delegates. Appointment Criteria Have a recognized degree or higher in Nursing, Social Sciences, Psychology or other related disciplines or an equivalent qualification; Have research knowledge related to, and skills in conducting quantitative studies; Proficiency in computer knowledge such as MS Office, SPSS Have a good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese; Have a good interpersonal and communication skills; and Be able to work independently. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/53/HL/RA) Duties The Research Assistants (1) will play a key role in supporting a research project \"Comparative Critical Discourse Analysis of Song Lyrics (1964 to 1969) alongside the British Invasion to the U.S. & Second-Wave Feminism Discourse-Historical Approach \" focusing on data analysis of the qualitative data from lyrics by following the introduced analytical framework; (2) will work closely with the Principal Investigator; (3) will be responsible for various tasks, including data analysis and drafting research manuscripts for presentation/publication in conferences/journals; (4) may be required to assist in other related tasks as needed; (5) display the ability to work independently and to demonstrate willingness to learn. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognized bachelor's degree or Sub-degree in any disciplines (preferably in Digital entertainment, IT or related disciplines concerning statistics); (b) research experience; (c) excellent communication and interpersonal skills; (d) positive attitude and ability to work well in a team; (e) proficiency in both written and spoken English; and (f) proficiency in computer applications. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Part-time Research Assistant, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/44/HL/RA) Duties The appointee will assist in the research project on: (a) administrative and coordinating work (b) collecting data and pre-processing them for experiments; (c) recruiting participants in experiments; (d) annotating data; (e) managing and updating datasets; (f) preparing reports; and (g) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a recognized Bachelor's degree in humanities field; (b) solid research experience; (c) excellent communication and interpersonal skills; (d) positive attitude and ability to work well in a team; (e) proficiency in both written and spoken English; and (f) proficiency in computer applications. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Full-time / Part-time Senior Research Assistant/Research Assistant, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/33/HS/RA) Duties The appointee will be responsible to assist with the administrative duties and conduction of the research project. Tasks include: (a) literature review; (b) making arrangement to ensure a smooth research study; (c) collecting data and conducting data analysis; (d) preparing publications and reports; and (e) performing other assigned duties. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) a bachelor's degree or above in health sciences or healthcare-related disciplines; (ii) 3-4 years of research experience and knowledge of mixed-methods research and survey design; (iii) knowledge in public health, community health and primary healthcare; (iv) a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; and (v) good interpersonal, organizational and communication skills.  Those with 3 years' relevant experience or more may be considered for appointment as Senior Research Assistant. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref.: 26/27/SS/RA) Duties The appointee will assist the Principal Investigator and the research team to support the research project. Duties include literature review, data collection and analysis, project management, report and manuscript writing and other related responsibilities as required. The appointee should be able to work independently and communicate in English and Chinese. Appointment Criteria Applicants should possess at least a bachelor's degree in social science or relevant disciplines, with proficiency in SPSS/R/Python and other computer software, have knowledge and research skills in both quantitative and qualitative research, and/or have relevant research experience. Appointment will be made on contract basis, which can be renewed thereafter subject to funds available. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Associate, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/20/HL/RA) Duties The appointees will be responsible for various tasks relating to the Chinese culture project, which include (a) coordinating research design; (b) overseeing data collection and analysis; (c) writing academic publications and reports; (d) editing book series and academic journals; (e) performing other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a doctoral degree in the humanities or relevant fields; (b) 3-4 years of research experience and knowledge of qualitative research; (c) strong background in research; (d) ability to work independently; (e) proficiency in writing in English and Chinese; (f) proficiency in communication and presentation skills. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/19/HL/RA) Duties The appointees will (a) assist the work of painting, drawing, animation, video production, and photography relating to the Chinese culture project; (b) assist the work of data collection and analysis; and (c) perform other duties as assigned. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (a) a bachelor's degree or master's degree in the humanities or relevant fields; (b) knowledge and skills of computer graphics; and (c) have good communication skills and sense of responsibility. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled Research Assistant, S School of Computing and Information Sciences (Ref.: 26/05/CIS/RA) We are seeking a highly motivated and talented individual to join our team as a Research Assistant for the project \"AI in telehealth\". Duties The appointee will be responsible (a) collect and analyze data to evaluate the performance of the wet electrostatic precipitators and propose improvements; (b) contribute to the publication of research findings in scientific journals and present results at conferences; (c) work closely with the project lead and team members to ensure the project's objectives are met; and (d) assist in the supervision and mentoring of undergraduate and graduate students involved in the project. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) a Bachelor's Degree in Computer Science, Information Technology or related disciplines; (ii) have experience in statistical data; (iii) be able to work independently; (iv) have good communication and interpersonal skills; and (v) have good English writing skills. Applicants with publication experience are preferred. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled"
